## Summary

`clearResponseHeaders(event)` with no name list should remove every response header. Right now it deletes from `event.res.headers` while looping over its live `keys()` iterator. Each delete shifts the remaining entries, so the header after each deleted one gets skipped and about half the headers are left behind.

```js
app.get("/", (event) => {
  event.res.headers.set("x-a", "1");
  event.res.headers.set("x-b", "2");
  event.res.headers.set("x-c", "3");
  event.res.headers.set("x-d", "4");
  clearResponseHeaders(event);
  return [...event.res.headers.keys()]; // ["x-b", "x-d"] on main
});
```

The fix copies the header names into an array before deleting. The `headerNames` path already worked.

Tests: new `clearResponseHeaders` cases in `test/utils.test.ts` (web + node matrix) cover clearing all headers, including multiple `set-cookie` entries, and clearing only named ones. The first case fails on `main` and passes with this change. `pnpm vitest run test/utils.test.ts` and `pnpm lint` pass.

_Found and fixed with help from an AI coding assistant. I reviewed the change and tests._


